    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Those accent marks aren't decoration — *kor* (\"age\") and *kór* (\"illness\") are different words. Hungarians hear vowel length the way English speakers hear the difference between \"bit\" and \"beat.\" Treat every *á*/*é*/*í*/*ó*/*ő*/*ú*/*ű* as its own letter, not a typo waiting to be ignored."
